## CMake / MSVC build trees. "build-*" catches the per-configuration trees
## (build-asym, build-auth); without it their .vcxproj and CTestTestfile.cmake
## are offered to git, and those name the self-test targets.
build/
build-*/
out/

## Visual Studio / VS Code local state
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo

## Build artefacts that may escape build/
*.obj
*.o
*.lib
*.a
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp

## No binaries are committed: the repository is source-only. A ready-to-run
## executable demo is published separately as a GitHub Release. See README.md.

## Editor / OS scratch
*.log
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

## Internal development history (not for publication)
HISTORY.md

## From doc/, only README.txt and the exported manual SOFA-UM-105.pdf are
## published (nothing here ignores doc/*.pdf, so the manual stays tracked).
## Everything else under doc/ is a working file, not for distribution.
doc/*.docx
doc/_archive/
doc/um105/
doc/decisions/

## Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

## The self-test suite is maintained separately and is not part of this
## distribution. CMakeLists.txt guards on tests/ existing, so a checkout
## without it configures and builds normally.
tests/
